# core.autocrlf is on globally on some machines, and `verify.py` hashes the text
# of every module against the digest the release recorded. One CRLF conversion on
# checkout makes all 1106 hashes fail, so the working copy is pinned to LF too.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.lean text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
